    "text": "I labelled 8 columns for job 1 and submitted them with report_profile.\n\n- `rx_claim_id`: identifier, PHI (claim ID, treated as potentially linkable to a person)\n- `member_id`: identifier, PHI\n- `fill_date`: date, PHI (fill date tied to an individual)\n- `ndc`: code, not PHI\n- `days_supply`: count, not PHI\n- `quantity`: count, not PHI\n- `paid_amount`: amount, not PHI\n- `pharmacy_npi`: identifier, not PHI (pharmacy provider ID, not a person's)\n\nThe `rx_claim_id`, `fill_date` and `pharmacy_npi` labels are judgement calls. I marked the claim ID and fill date as PHI under the \"when unsure, mark it\" rule, and treated the pharmacy NPI as a provider identifier rather than a person's.\n\n8 columns labelled.",
